  "result": "`satisfies(version, range)` is now implemented in `src/semver.js` following `docs/SPEC.md`, and `npm test` passes (5 tests, 0 failed).\n\nThe new tests are in `test/semver.test.js`. They cover:\n- every example row in the spec (X-ranges, tilde, caret, hyphen ranges, `||`);\n- the prerelease rule and prerelease ordering;\n- build metadata being ignored;\n- invalid versions, invalid ranges and non-string input, all of which return `false`.\n\nThe spec leaves a few cases open, so I chose these behaviors:\n- **Wildcards with an operator:** `>*` and `<*` match nothing, while `>=*`, `<=*` and `=*` match any non-prerelease version.\n- **Wildcard before a number:** a range like `1.x.3` is invalid and returns `false`.\n- **Empty `||` branch:** an empty branch such as `\"1.2.3 ||\"` counts as \"any version\", following the spec's \"`*` or empty\".",
